  "notes": "ぐつぐつ is an onomatopoeia for the sound and appearance of liquid simmering steadily in a pot.\n\nGRAMMAR:\nUsed with と (ぐつぐつと) or directly before a verb:\n- ぐつぐつと{煮|に}る: to simmer\n- ぐつぐつ{煮込|にこ}む: to stew, to simmer down\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ぐつぐつ{煮|に}える: to be simmering\n- {鍋|なべ}がぐつぐつ{言|い}う: the pot is bubbling\n- ぐつぐつと{音|おと}を{立|た}てる: to make bubbling sounds\n\nRELATED COOKING ONOMATOPOEIA (from gentle to vigorous):\n- ことこと: gentle simmering (lighter, quieter)\n- ぐつぐつ: moderate, steady simmer\n- ふつふつ: just starting to bubble\n- ぐらぐら: rolling boil (vigorous, strong bubbling)\n\nぐつぐつ suggests sustained bubbling at medium heat — not as gentle as ことこと, but not as violent as ぐらぐら.",
